== the default session selector:
interactive
== --tab-selector plain:
plain
== --tab-selector external:
external
== --dumb selects plain:
plain
== an explicit value wins over --dumb:
interactive
== an unknown command line value is rejected:
1:16: error: Unknown --tab-selector value, expected one of 'interactive', 'external', or 'plain'.
     1 |  --tab-selector bogus
       |                 ^~~~~
status=2
== koshconf changes it at runtime:
external
== a mood change keeps the selector:
plain
== an unknown koshconf value is rejected:
-c:1:41: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Invalid value 'bogus' for 'kosh.completion.menu_style', expected 'interactive', 'external', or 'plain'.
     1 |  koshconf set kosh.completion.menu_style bogus
       |                                          ^~~~~
status=1
== set no longer accepts the long form:
-c:1:5: error: Builtin `set`: Unknown option '--tab-selector'.
     1 |  set --tab-selector plain
       |      ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Use koshconf for Koshka settings without a letter, such as `koshconf set kosh.mood bash`.
status=1
== the selector survives a subshell:
external
